summary:
  moveWhen says now whatever the old address's time of death.

history:
  The rule the commit asks. With it gone every identity-proven candidate is
  written at once again, which is the behaviour the five minutes were added to
  end.

target:
  package/contents/ui/HealLogic.js

find:
      return firstDeadMs > 0 && dead >= DEATH_PROOF_MS ? "now" : "later";

replace:
      return "now";

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_heallogic.qml::test_a_move_is_written_only_over_an_address_that_stayed_dead.
  Line-neutral.
